description:
Implement the NAMESPACE command (RFC 2342) in crates/imap/src/session/mailbox.rs and wire it into the dispatch loop in mod.rs.

Algorithm:
1. In mailbox.rs, add: pub fn handle_namespace() -> Data<'static>
   - personal: vec![Namespace::new(IString::try_from("").expect("empty string is valid IString"), Some(QuotedChar::try_from('.').expect("dot is valid QuotedChar")))]
   - other: vec![]
   - shared: vec![]
   - return Data::namespace(personal, vec![], vec![]).expect("valid namespace args")
2. In mod.rs, add CommandBody::Namespace arm before the _ => catch-all (currently around line 514):
   CommandBody::Namespace => match ctx.state {
       ImapState::Authenticated { .. } | ImapState::Selected { .. } => {
           server.enqueue_data(handle_namespace());
           server.enqueue_status(Status::ok(Some(tag), None, "NAMESPACE complete").expect("static ok"));
       }
       _ => { /* send NO */ }
   },
3. Add handle_namespace to the use mailbox::{...} import in mod.rs.
4. All types (Namespace, IString, QuotedChar) are available after ext_namespace feature is enabled.

Defensive rules: NAMESPACE must be rejected in NotAuthenticated state with tagged NO. No user input is reflected in the NAMESPACE response — hardcoded values only.

Acceptance: cargo test -p stoa-imap passes; new unit tests (separate bead) verify response structure and wrong-state rejection.
